temu; teensy eensy markup language
==================================

temu (teensy eensy markup language; or temu markdown) is a lightweight markup 
language designed to be as close to a .txt file as possible. provided is a 
converter from temu to html, written in c for POSIX systems

temu features
-------------

the heading you just read is a feature. lines underlined with hyphens are
converted to h2s, and lines underlined with equals are converted to h1s.

we have `code!` it supports both inline and

`not

inline!`

we also have
	blockquotes! you can add a tab before your paragraph to make it a
	blockquote instead of a paragraph. not every line of the blockquote
	has to be tab indented, although they can be,
	it does mean that there must be whitespace between a tab indented
	line and a line intended not to be,

like this.

we also have https://links.faketld ! hyperlinks (currently) arent supported.
you can link to a file on your own website like ://file.txt , and you can
make the link be wrapped in an <img> by replacing the colon with a !, like
https!//en.topreism.org/itm/ND01N0top.png .

